1. State change ho
Jab useState ya useReducer se state update hoti hai.
const [count, setCount] = useState(0);

return <button onClick={() => setCount(count + 1)}>{count}</button>;


Button click par count change hoga, toh component re-render hoga.
2. Parent component re-render ho
Parent re-render hota hai toh uske child components bhi normally re-render hote hain, chahe props change na hon. React.memo kuch cases mein unnecessary child re-renders skip kar sakta hai.
3. Context ki value change ho
Agar component useContext se kisi Context ko use kar raha hai aur us Context ki value change hoti hai, toh component re-render hota hai.

Props change hon: Child ko naye props milne par woh usually re-render hota hai.

useRef ki value change ho: Sirf ref.current change karne se re-render nahi hota.

Normal variable change ho: Usse bhi automatically re-render nahi hota.

useEffect chale: Effect chalne se apne aap re-render nahi hota; lekin effect ke andar state update ho toh ho sakta hai.